data
  title annotation vs as vs satisfies: safety x precision
  desc Two axes — does it run a real check, and does it keep the precise inferred type? Only satisfies wins both corners; the no-check + precise corner has no tool.
  compares
    - label Annotation — checks, but widens
    - label satisfies — checks and keeps type
    - label as — no check, also widens
    - label Precise without check — impossible
